<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

Explanation:
- `\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result` ensures that we are considering all valid indices up to the new length of the BitSet after setting the bit.
- `i != bitIndex` ensures that we exclude the bit at `bitIndex` since it is the one being changed.
- `this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i))` ensures that the value of the bit at index `i` remains unchanged before and after the operation.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.length() && i != bitIndex; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
